import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'..')
from con_helpers import *
save(3,3,"Saṁskāra as a Live Filter: How Conditioning Shapes Every Perception","Think of one reaction of yours that rang longer or louder than the event deserved. What was its shape: the overshoot, the settling time or the ripple?",[
mc("U","Two people hear the same slightly sharp remark. One barely notices it; the other is shaken for hours. According to Conversation 3.3, what does this show?",
 ["The shaken person has heard the words more accurately and taken them in more honestly.","The shaken person has a weaker character, which steady effort can slowly strengthen.","How big the ring is and how long it lasts belongs to each mind’s signature, not to the remark.","The remark was struck harder for one of them, because tone carries more than words do."],2,
 "Strike two bells with the same tap and each answers in its own way: how high it overshoots, how long it rings and the faint after-hum are the bell’s signature, not the tap’s. The mind has a signature too, so the same remark can barely touch one person and floor another.",
 "The size and length of a reaction belong to the mind’s signature, not to the event","Part 1"),
mc("A","A teacher notices that after a mild criticism she is still turning it over hours later, long after her colleagues have moved on. Which view fits Conversation 3.3?",
 ["Her ring runs long, a pattern she can come to know and soften, and no fault to confess.","Reactions that last this long show a lack of self-control, which she should work to stop.","She should avoid every situation where criticism might come, so the bell is never struck.","The criticism must have been serious, since a reaction lasts as long as its cause demands."],0,
 "The three things to watch are the overshoot, the settling time and the ripple, and recognising them is not a fault to confess: it is the instrument coming to know itself. A long settling time is a signature that can be softened, not a verdict on the person.",
 "Knowing your own ring is the first step to softening it, with no blame","Part 1"),
mc("A","A father’s reactions to his child’s tantrums are big and last for hours. Using the car-suspension picture, which view fits Conversation 3.3?",
 ["Tantrums are the bumps, so the work is to prevent them, and then the car will never bounce.","The worn-out suspension cannot be mended, so he should accept that his reactions will ring on.","He should treat each bounce as proof that he is not a good enough parent for the child.","Bumps will come in any life; the work is to change the suspension, and that can be done."],3,
 "Life has bumps. The work is not to stop hitting them but to change the suspension. What softens the ring: living by your values, seeing a situation clearly, slow breathing, calm unhurried time, and above all coming to know your own pattern.",
 "Change the suspension, not the bumps: what softens the ring","Part 1"),
mc("A","A teacher gives the same honest feedback to two students. One thinks, “Useful, I can fix this.” The other thinks, “They have always doubted me.” Which explanation fits Conversation 3.3?",
 ["The second student chose, in that moment, to read the words in a harsh way.","Each past had already coloured the words: one filter says information, the other verdict.","The second student did not read the feedback carefully and should be asked to read it again.","The teacher’s tone must have changed between the two, so the words were not really the same."],1,
 "The words were the same. What differed was the filter each student’s past had laid over them before they finished reading. Neither is choosing in that instant; each is receiving the world already shaped.",
 "The past colours the words before we finish reading them","Part 2"),
judge("“By the time a reaction is felt, the filter has already coloured the moment, so there is nothing a person can do about it.”",P,
 "The colouring happens before perception, and usually it cannot be stopped at that first instant. But a breath later the clear-seeing part of the mind can catch it: “this feeling of being attacked is my filter, not a fact about this person.” That crack is where everything later becomes possible.",
 "The first colouring is usually too early to stop, but it can be noticed a breath later","Part 2"),
mc("A","A mother, a breath after a comment, notices that she feels attacked by the speaker. Which step fits Conversation 3.3?",
 ["Decide that the comment was neutral, because it was probably meant kindly.","See that the feeling is her filter at work, not a fact about this person.","Push the feeling away at once, so that it cannot colour what she hears next.","Trust the feeling as a reliable signal, since it arrived so quickly and so strongly."],1,
 "The first freedom is simply noticing the glasses are on. The tint is already inside the seeing, so telling someone to just see it differently often fails; but noticing the filter breaks the spell of “this is simply how things are.”",
 "Noticing the filter, the tinted glasses, is the first freedom","Part 2"),
judge("“The past is stored like a filing cabinet with a folder for each event, and a smell simply helps a person find the right folder.”",F,
 "The past is stored not as folders filed by date but as a pattern, a signature spread through the mind. Any present cue that shares the signature, a scent, a bar of a song, a tone, strikes it and the whole pattern reassembles at once: picture, feeling, body and meaning. The past is rebuilt, not recalled.",
 "Memory is a signature that is rebuilt by a matching cue, not a folder that is opened","Part 3"),
mc("A","A patient is flooded with fear when she smells antiseptic. Following Conversation 3.3, how might a doctor help in the moment?",
 ["Tell her the fear is irrational, so that she can stop reacting to it at once.","Help her avoid antiseptic smells for good, so that the pattern is never struck again.","Offer the thought that an old pattern is reassembling, not present danger, with slow breaths.","Ask her to recall the whole original event in detail while the fear is at its height."],2,
 "The freeing move is to recognise a reassembly: “this pattern is active right now, and it is real as a pattern, but I am not back there.” Paired with slow breaths, the calmer state mixes into the memory as it is revisited, and what is stored is a little kinder than before.",
 "Recognise an old pattern reassembling, and pair it with a calm state","Part 3"),
mc("U","According to the riverbed picture, what is true of a conditioned pattern (saṁskāra)?",
 ["It is deeply grooved, but not concrete: a steady change of flow can slowly re-carve it.","It was set in the early years and, once set, it can be understood but never really changed.","It is carved only by the present moment, so the past leaves no channel in the mind.","It can be filled in at once by deciding firmly to react in a different way from now on."],0,
 "A riverbed is not concrete. Change the flow steadily, in direction and in force, and over time old channels silt up and new ones deepen. It works through catching the filter in the act, repeating a new response, a non-grabbing watchfulness, and the steadying practices. Patiently, not at once.",
 "A saṁskāra is deeply grooved and still changeable, patiently","Part 4"),
judge("“A person whose filter amplifies shame can learn to hear the kind voice as clearly as the harsh one, as true, kind and accurate experiences that the old filter did not predict are laid down.”",T,
 "None of these filters is a verdict on the person, and every one is teachable. The shame filter can learn to hear the kind voice as clearly as the harsh one: each true, kind, accurate experience that the old filter did not predict helps carve a new channel.",
 "Each filter is teachable: new, true experience helps carve a new channel","Part 4")])
